# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# SABSIM .gitignore
#
# Two kinds of things are excluded here: ordinary build/tooling debris
# that no repository should carry, and a small set of local-only working
# files we deliberately keep out of the public repository (raw session
# transcripts, a copyrighted reference PDF, and the early planning notes
# whose content has already been folded into the dev/ document chain).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python bytecode caches and packaging debris.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Test-runner cache.
.pytest_cache/

# LAMMPS run debris. LAMMPS writes log.lammps into the CURRENT directory
# unless told otherwise, so a driver run started from the repo root drops
# one here. Real runs redirect it into the job directory on scratch
# (`-log <job_dir>/log.<tag>`); this rule catches the stragglers.
log.lammps
log.cite

# Job working directories — run output, never project source. Each job
# directory holds an `intermediate` symlink into the SABSIM_SCRATCH
# mirror (see sabsim/deploy/scratch.py) plus whatever the run drops
# beside it; the bytes themselves live on scratch. Nothing here needs to
# be tracked for a run to be reproducible, because the manifest records
# the RESOLVED scratch path rather than relying on the link.
/jobs/

# The `intermediate` scratch symlink is dropped in WHATEVER directory a
# run is launched from (the run's home is the CWD), so ignore the reserved
# link name anywhere — including a stray one from running in the repo root.
intermediate

# Machine-local Claude Code settings (permissions allowlist, etc.).
# The shared skills under .claude/commands/ ARE tracked; only the
# per-machine settings file is ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Machine-local deployment rc holding the three root variables
# (SABSIM_SCRATCH / SABSIM_SHARE / SABSIM_LOCAL, ARCHITECTURE.md §4.1).
# The installer generates it inside the clone at .sabsim/sabsimrc and the
# user edits it to match their machine, so it is per-checkout state, not
# project source — like settings.local.json above.
.sabsim/

# Raw session transcripts and the helper that reflows them. These are
# working logs, not project deliverables, so they stay local.
conversation.txt
conversation-readable.txt
*-local-command-caveat*.txt
reflow_transcript.py

# Copyrighted reference article (Kulichenko et al. 2023, UDD). Kept
# local to avoid redistributing it; the design chain cites it instead.
*.pdf

# Early planning notes. Their relevant content has been migrated into
# dev/VISION.md and dev/ARCHITECTURE.md; kept local for later mining.
onboarding-overview.md
imago-session-summary.md

# Retired design/planning docs, moved out of the way (the old HANDOFF.md,
# session transcripts, and reference PDFs). Kept locally for reference but
# no longer useful enough to track.
dev/old_docs/

# A student's wafer-bonding pipeline, dropped in for study (two drops:
# sunita/ and the newer sunita2/ with a built amorphization stage). Not
# part of the SABSIM source tree; the reusable assets and deficiencies
# are catalogued in dev/PRIOR_ART.md (§1.6-§1.9), which is what the
# repository actually carries. Kept local so we can mine it without
# vendoring someone else's project.
sunita/
sunita2/

# Editor scratch files. A vim swap file was staged once because the note
# it belonged to was open while committing; ignoring the pattern is
# cheaper than remembering to look.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
